OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G2/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A train driver died and more than 50
OL,6, people were injured when two trains
OL,7, collided in Staffordshire yesterday.
OL,9,FThe dead man was Mr E Goode from Crewe,
OL,10,Faged in his fifties. Four people are
OL,11,Fcritically or seriously ill and being
OL,12,Fthreated in an intensive care unit.
OL,14,FBR said the 17.00 Euston-Manchester and
OL,15,Fthe 17.20 Liverpool-Euston struck one
OL,16,Fanother a glancing blow at Colwick
OL,17,FJunction then derailed.
OL,19,FThe southbound train was travelling at
OL,20,F90-100mph, the other at 50-60mph. BR
OL,21,Fhas begun an internal ingestigation.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18103
SC,0003
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789941877
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G3/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The general manager of British Rail's
OL,6, London-Midland Region said about 800
OL,7, people were on the two trains which
OL,8, collided at Colwich Junction.
OL,10,FMr Cyril Bleasdale said more would have
OL,11,Fbeen injured if the carriages had not
OL,12,Fbeen relatively modern.
OL,14,FHe said he understood both trains were
OL,15,Fon time and that the train from
OL,16,FLiverpool should have cleared the
OL,17,Fjunction before the train from Euston.
OL,19,FModern electric-lighting signalling was
OL,20,Fused on the stretch of track and there
OL,21,Fwas a signal box about 60 yards from
OL,22,Fthe crash site, he added.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 20-09-86
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18104
SC,0004
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789941877
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     GG4/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The general manager of British Rail's
OL,6, London-Midland Region said a second man
OL,7, was travelling in the cab of one of the
OL,8, trains in yesterday's rail crash.
OL,10,FMr Cyril Bleasdale said the man was in
OL,11,Fthe cab of the Euston to Manchester
OL,12,Fexpress. He and the driver jumped from
OL,13,Fthe cab seconds before the collision.
OL,15,FThe man is understood to have been a
OL,16,FBR employee - in some cases they are
OL,17,Fauthorised to travel with the driver.
OL,19,FOf the 52 injured in the crash, 32 are
OL,20,Fstill in hospital.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
