CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789941877
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, US-Soviet talks on a possible summit
OL,6, have resumed in Washington, with the
OL,7, Daniloff affair still casting a shadow
OL,8, over the proceedings.
OL,10,FYesterday President Reagan had an
OL,11,Funscheduled meeting with Soviet foreign
OL,12,Fminister Mr Eduard Shevardnadze.
OL,14,FToday Mr Shevardnadze continued talks
OL,15,Fwith US Secretary of State Mr George
OL,16,FShultz.
OL,18,FThey are said to be working on a four-
OL,19,Fpoint summit agenda, consisting of arms
OL,20,Fcontrol, regional issues, humanitarian
OL,21,Fquestions and bilateral affiars.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18109
SC,0009
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789941877
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Soviet Communist Party newspaper
OL,6, Pravda says the US is using Nicholas
OL,7, Daniloff's arrest to frustrate a new
OL,8, superpower summit.
OL,10,FPravda echoed Soviet leader Mr Mikhail
OL,11,FGorbachev in calling journalist
OL,12,FNicholas Daniloff a spy and said there
OL,13,Fhad been an "escalation of anti-
OL,14,FSovietism" over the affair.
OL,16,FThis, the paper said, was part of a
OL,17,Fpattern of behaviour by the US "to
OL,18,Ffrustrate a possible summit and pass
OL,19,Fthe blame for it onto Moscow".
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18110
SC,0010
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789941877
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/10
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, There have been two bomb attacks aimed
OL,6, at Roman Catholic families in Northern
OL,7, Ireland.
OL,9,FA Catholic home in Dunmurry, County
OL,10,FAntrim was petrol-bombed. There was
OL,11,Fsome damage and the owner of the
OL,12,Fhouse suffered minor burns.
OL,14,FA small booby-trap bomb went off behind
OL,15,Fa house belonging to a Catholic family
OL,16,Fin the Waterside area of Londonderry.
OL,17,FNo-one was injured.
OL,19,S/FPolice are still questioning eight
OL,20,Fmen about a series of recent sectarian
OL,21,Fmurders in north Belfast.
OL,23,T]CFrom 20-09-86   teletextarchive.com
